    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d439">

                <pb facs="0554" n="486" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v01/pg486"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.11 Se 8/48</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to President Wilson </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-10-08">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 8, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. President</hi>: I enclose an instruction
                    to our Ambassador at Berlin relative to the <hi rendition="#italic">William P.
                        Frye</hi> case.<anchor n="65" xml:id="d439-f1"/> It is in response <pb
                        facs="0555" n="487" xml:id="pg487"/> to the German note on the subject dated
                    September 19—the original of which I also enclose.<anchor n="66"
                        xml:id="d439-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>You will perceive that we accept the proposal for a joint commission of experts
                    to fix the amount of indemnity and also agree to submit to arbitration the
                    controversy as to the interpretation of the Treaty of 1828. As the submission to
                    arbitration will be by <hi rendition="#italic">compromis</hi> it will be
                    necessary to lay it before the Senate for their consent. For this reason I am
                    troubling you with the matter.</p>
                <p>I believe the course proposed in the telegram to be advisable, as it will close
                    the interchange of notes on the subject.</p>
                <p>Faithfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d439-f1" n="65" xml:id="d439-f1-content">
                <p>For the instruction as sent, see <ref target="frus1915Supp#pg_570">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1915, supp., p.
